=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
The affected component is the VLAN 6 switched virtual interface (SVI) on sshswitch, which acts as the inter-VLAN routing layer-3 switch for Campus 2. sshswitch bridges VLAN-tagged traffic from switch4 (carrying VLAN 5 for PC1/PC2/dc_pc5 and VLAN 6 for PC3/PC4) through bond0 sub-interfaces and exposes per-VLAN bridge interfaces (br_v5, br_v6, etc.) as default gateways.

The mechanism of failure is straightforward: PC3 and PC4 are correctly configured with default gateway 10.6.0.254/24, but the sshswitch bridge interface br_v6 has been assigned the wrong IP address — 10.6.0.200/24 instead of 10.6.0.254/24. When PC3/PC4 ARP for 10.6.0.254, no device in the broadcast domain answers, producing "Destination Host Unreachable" for every packet. No other router (e.g., router17) holds a 10.6.0.x address, confirming there is no alternative gateway.

VLAN 5 is unaffected because its SVI br_v5 is correctly set to 10.5.0.254/24, matching what PC1/PC2/dc_pc5 use, and ping from PC1 to 10.5.0.254 succeeds without issue.

Root cause: sshswitch's br_v6 (VLAN 6 SVI) was misconfigured with IP 10.6.0.200/24 instead of the required 10.6.0.254/24.

Corrective fix: On sshswitch, remove the incorrect address and assign the correct one:
  ip addr del 10.6.0.200/24 dev br_v6
  ip addr add 10.6.0.254/24 dev br_v6
Then persist the fix in the Kathara startup script for sshswitch.
=== END ===
```